<title>FRANCE: Renault 1996 net loss 5.2 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Renault 1996 net loss 5.2 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable loss		   5,248 vs profit 2,139</p>
<p>    Net dividend				none  vs 3.50</p>
<p>    Net loss				    5,266 vs profit 2,281</p>
<p>    Loss before taxes			 5,645 vs profit 1,976</p>
<p>    Operating loss			    5,987 vs profit 1,259</p>
<p>    Net financial profit			324 vs profit   654</p>
<p>    Turnover				  184,078 vs 184,065</p>
<p>    Investment (billion francs)	  16.39  vs 15.26</p>
<p>    Net debt (billion francs)	     9.39  vs 3.37</p>
<p>    Shareholding funds (billion Ffr)   37.77  vs 43.80</p>
<p>NOTE - Renault gave the results in a statement. Chairman Louis Schweitzer told reporters he expected Renault to show an operating profit in 1997. &quot;The net result will depend on exceptional items,&quot; he said.  </p>
<p>The full 1996 loss included 3.91 billion francs in charges for the planned closure of Belgium's Vilvoorde plant and planned job cuts in France.</p>
</text>
